  "mathematical_checks": {
    "CC9": "Verified v=log u>=1, T=exp(sqrt v) in [2,u], T^(-1)<=E, uE>=1, and the factor-three denominator comparison. The complete zero sum and every explicit-formula error are bounded by the claimed common uE(lambda+v)^2 majorant. Constants depend only on the preceding real-zero margin, not on conductor or height.",
    "CC10": "Matched the full psi_thin quantifier order at PsiThin.lean385-421: c0 precedes C,c, which precede primitive chi, N, lambda and u. The real nonprincipal NoExc premise remains; principal primitive N=1 and nonreal characters are handled without inventing a zero-free critical strip.",
    "CC11": "The fixed-modulus finite minimum supplies only a fixed-character real-zero margin. The exp(-c sqrt(log u)) bound absorbs the required log powers; deleted Euler factors contribute O_N(log u). Local boundedness and the integrable 1/(u log^2 u) tail prove absolute integrability of psi0/u^2 without importing a uniform Siegel-Walfisz estimate.",
    "CC12": "Recomputed finite Abel summation with the full floor convention, the A(U)/U limit, and dominated convergence for sigma down to one. The resulting series is convergent, not absolutely convergent, and its sum is -L_prime(1)/L(1). The centered ramp has the exact plus y L_prime/L sign and equals -y times the tail integral.",
    "CC13": "Recomputed -zeta_prime/zeta(sigma)-sigma/(sigma-1), whose Laurent limit is -1-gamma, not merely -gamma. The finite integral and tail subtraction reproduce exactly y(log y-1-gamma) in the principal centering. The primitive principal restriction removes deleted Euler factors.",
    "CC14": "Checked source G0, gChi_ne, gChi_one, one_apply_of_primitive, l21a, g_integral and gauss_sum_function_eq. On 1<=n<=floor y the max equals y/n-1. The principal and nonprincipal formulas and sign conventions match the actual functions used by ThinH.",
    "CC15": "Checked both exact exponent gaps: 61/300-1/5=1/300 and 13/100-1/8=1/200. The bound lambda<=v^(61/100) is uniform over v>=log y; the substitution u=exp(v) cancels the u factor and yields the stated tail. Splitting the exponential produces a finite fixed K_c and absorbs any prescribed c_prime. Measurable integrands are genuinely integrable; the totalized-integral convention separately handles the source theorem without a measurability premise.",
    "CC16": "Matched Thin.lean10-49. Taking lambda=max(1,log N) costs A+1 only, and a single enlarged x0 enforces y>=e and all previous inequalities. The threshold precedes every primitive chi, N and every y above the cutoff; no choice depending on y or chi is introduced.",
    "CC17": "Checked odd-prime principal-unit p-groups, the square-root lifting step z to z+2^(j-1) at 2 (valid for j>=3), CRT descent and primitivity. These give the exact v_p(N)<=1 for odd p and v_2(N)<=3, hence N divides M q d under the original prime-support assumptions. No analogous restriction is asserted for nonreal characters.",
    "CC18": "Matched SmallZeros.lean32-45 for all nonprincipal characters modulo every positive N<=B0. Finiteness and continuity at one yield one positive radius, including the empty bounded set. Reality and primitivity are not smuggled into this stronger bounded-modulus scope, and no uniform unbounded-conductor Siegel estimate is asserted.",
    "CC19": "Checked HostRaw.IsCharE -> N divides condN through the actual primitive inducer (level_dvd47-53), condN=QS*q*d, the odd-part bound and the two cases q|N or d|N. RealBox supplies precisely the first case; quadratic conductor restriction and the bounded-modulus exclusion supply the second. The outer constant is 1, the threshold depends only on B and epsilon, and the final text explicitly retains 0<epsilon<1/52. HC9 is a consumer, not a dependency. RealBox construction, PairEx and relative prime-progression estimates remain separate.",
    "CC20": "Differentiated the exact tail identity and checked the plus signs in G_prime=psi0/y+G0/y. Each finite ramp is continuous at integers; the right derivative uses the full floor sum, and local absolute continuity justifies integration across the jumps in the derivative. The same tail exponent gap gives a pointwise psi0/y estimate, with 2b absorbing the sum of two terms. This is correctly labeled an additional late-cutoff consequence, not the source polynomial-window square-root estimate."
  },
